{"body":{"asks":"Layers as OpenLight drew them, content and an overlay above it, a kiosk perhaps otherwise, any kind of layer with any implementation; the expression input's completion menu and the context menu its first overlays. The author wants the idea scrutinised. The agents leaned completion to the input's own popover instead, which he holds the absolute opposite of what was drawn, to be grounded further and taken apart.","awaits":true,"raised":[{"$ref":"1M88X8HVYZRC002"}],"stands":"leaning"},"id":"1M88X8HVYZRC00C","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Layers and overlays"}
{"body":{"asks":"Whatever is mounted in a slot is agnostic and decoupled, and implements no chrome. The parent giving the card and background, a component being its content, seemed to the author smart and sane, though nesting troubles it; or the slot gives it; he cannot quite grasp it yet. A focus ring and a selection are chrome too, as OpenLight's reader gave collation selections their colours, whose shape whatever draws them may not know, and themes differ: perhaps a framework way of splicing into the holarchy. The agents leaned to the host and the look; the author trusts it not yet.","awaits":true,"raised":[{"$ref":"1M88X8HVYZRC004"}],"stands":"open"},"id":"1M88X8HVYZRC00E","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Chrome around nested components"}
{"body":{"asks":"A component in code that draws a holon in its own markup, as Value a card and prose a link, hides it from the chassis, which knows only that Value drew there; the inspector reads attributes the components set to find it. Layout as data has no such gap. The author: perhaps components in code have a way to declare what something is, so that it is available; the session: or they place whatever shows a holon by io.draw, drawing only what is no holon themselves.","awaits":true,"raised":[{"$ref":"1M88X8HVYZRC008"}],"stands":"open"},"id":"1M88X8HVYZRC00J","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Holons drawn inside components in code"}
{"body":{"asks":"Agents sent with a session's narrow brief argued its framing, read Knowledge in part and agreed as one. Perhaps they are to bootstrap themselves properly, each with a degree of free will, exploring without constraint, carrying a culture of exploration, critique and digestion. Sent alike, do they all do the same, or spread by chance? Steering them or siloing them by topic does not quite resonate with the author; their first talking among themselves he has not tried and doubts. Perhaps three sent completely free first, their results then weighed.","awaits":true,"raised":[{"$ref":"1M88X8HVYZRC009"}],"stands":"open"},"id":"1M88X8HVYZRC00K","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Free agents and their orchestration"}